    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d811">

                <pb facs="0709" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg699"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/6–1449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-14T16:00:00+01:00">June 14, 1949—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 14—2:58 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>216. Foreign Minister<anchor n="59" xml:id="d811-f1"/> assured me this morning
                    that Portuguese Minister Canton has been instructed to conform actions to those
                    of US and UK colleagues (infotel June 13, 4 a.m.<anchor n="58" xml:id="d811-f2"
                    />); if move made to Hong Kong, Minister will leave Consul [in] Canton to take
                    care of Portuguese nationals.</p>
                <p>Expressed special interest US efforts encourage western powers continue contact
                    with Chinese Government and reiterated his belief in supreme importance
                    concerted attitude (mytel 187, May 19<anchor n="60" xml:id="d811-f3"/>).</p>
                <pb facs="0710" n="700" xml:id="pg700"/>
                <p>Added that following apparent crystallization British intention hold Hong Kong
                    Portuguese Government sending four battalions of approximately 1,000 each to
                    Macau, to reinforce present garrison of 2,000 plus 1,000 armed police. Two of
                    new battalions will be Portuguese and two African native.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
